event: section
data: {"type":"section","phase":"writer","sectionIndex":5,"sectionTitle":"Mounting Your Phone Alongside Your Fish Finder","sectionContent":"## Mounting Your Phone Alongside Your Fish Finder\n\nIf you're like most anglers today, your fish finder isn't the only screen on the water. You're probably running a navigation app, checking weather radar, tracking tournament stats, or just keeping your phone accessible for photos when you land something worth bragging about.\n\nThe good news: iBOLT's modular system means you don't need to buy into a completely separate mounting ecosystem for your phone. Since our parts use industry-standard ball sizes compatible with Garmin ball mount setups, you can add a phone mount right alongside your fish finder using the same rail or a nearby mounting point.\n\nThe [iBOLT Moto-Vise Heavy Duty Phone Handlebar/Rail Mount](https://iboltmounts.com/products/ibolt-moto-vise-heavy-duty-phone-handlebar-rail-mount) clamps directly to rails and tubing, making it perfect for T-track setups and kayak rails. Need a more permanent solution? The [iBOLT sPro2 AMPS Drill Base](https://iboltmounts.com/products/ibolt-spro2-amps-drill-base-phone-and-tablet-mounting-solution) lets you mount your phone to any flat surface on your console or deck using a standard AMPS hole pattern. For rougher conditions, the [Moto-Vise IncrediBOLT Handlebar/Rail Mount](https://iboltmounts.com/products/ibolt-moto-vise-incredibolt-heavy-duty-phone-clamp-handlebar-rail-mount) adds extra vibration resistance and a stronger grip that holds tight through chop and wake.\n\nOne cockpit, one modular system, every screen exactly where you need it."}

event: status
data: {"type":"status","phase":"writer","message":"Writing section 7/7: \"Picking the Best Garmin Fish Finder Mount for Your Setup\""}

event: section
data: {"type":"section","phase":"writer","sectionIndex":6,"sectionTitle":"Picking the Best Garmin Fish Finder Mount for Your Setup","sectionContent":"## Picking the Best Garmin Fish Finder Mount for Your Setup\n\nFinding the best Garmin fish finder mount really comes down to four decisions. First, identify your Garmin model and its mounting pattern. Second, determine your mounting surface: is it a rail, a flat deck, or a track system? Third, choose your ball size based on device weight. Lighter units like the Striker 4 do well on 25mm setups, while larger Garmin displays need 38mm (C size) support. Fourth, decide between a clamp base for non-permanent installs or a drill base for a locked-in position.\n\nThe [iBOLT Universal Marine Electronics Mounting Plate](https://iboltmounts.com/products/ibolt-universal-marine-electronics-mounting-plate) is a great starting point, giving you a versatile connection between your Garmin and any industry-standard ball arm. Every iBOLT mount ships within 24 business hours and is backed by a 2-year warranty.\n\nExplore the full iBOLT marine mounting lineup to find the right combination for your boat or kayak."}

