data: {"type":"verified","phase":"verifier","verification":{"brandConsistency":90,"seoOptimization":88,"naturalLanguage":91,"factualAccuracy":80,"overallScore":87,"issues":["The post frames iBOLT's marine line as an extension of its industrial/commercial expertise, which is good, but the marine product category is less established in the brand guidelines. The post could more strongly emphasize the specialist positioning ('purpose-built for specific industries') rather than just bridging from commercial to marine.","The Garmin Striker 4 weight is stated as 'approximately 0.5 lbs for the head unit alone,' which should be verified for accuracy. The actual Striker 4 weighs roughly 0.5 lbs (230g), so this appears correct but the hedging with 'approximately' is appropriate.","Some product URLs and Shopify image URLs contain suspicious version parameters (v=1770421453) that appear identical across all images, which may indicate placeholder or fabricated URLs rather than verified live links.","The meta title is 56 characters ('Best Garmin Fish Finder Mount | Striker 4, Vivid & ECHOMAP'), which is within the 60-character limit but could be tighter.","The post is approximately 1,800-2,000 words including the FAQ section, which exceeds the 800-1,400 word target range specified in the guidelines.","The comparison table lists 'LiveScope bundles' as compatible with specific mount types, but no iBOLT LiveScope-specific mount is referenced or linked, which could create unverifiable expectations."],"suggestions":["Trim the post to fall within the 800-1,400 word target. The FAQ section, while valuable for SEO, pushes the word count well over the limit. Consider condensing the FAQs to 3-4 questions or shortening answers.","Verify all product URLs and image URLs are live and accurate before publishing. The identical version parameters on all image URLs are a red flag.","Add a brief mention of the 2-year warranty and 24-hour shipping earlier in the post rather than only in the conclusion, as these are key brand differentiators that support trust-building throughout the piece.","Clarify or remove the LiveScope references unless iBOLT has verified compatibility and weight-bearing specs for LiveScope bundles, which can be significantly heavier than standard fish finders.","The specialist positioning could be sharpened. Rather than just saying 'iBOLT is known for building industrial-grade mounting systems,' consider a line that draws a clearer contrast: other mount brands sell generic hardware adapted for marine use, while iBOLT engineers purpose-built solutions based on real-world conditions.","Consider adding internal links to the Mount Configurator tool if it supports marine product selection, as this is a key brand differentiator mentioned in the guidelines."],"passesQualityGate":true},"message":"Re-verified: 87/100 (PASS)"}

